#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Fixing a sent-back record: only the flagged fields can change.
On a record that was sent back, fields the reviewers passed are locked for the extractor. Open: fields with a reviewer finding (open or
confirmed), a correction/SOP comment about the value that was sent back, or a rejection note on that field. A general note alone flags
nothing, so then every field stays open. Admins are never limited. Applies to the record editor, the JSON editor and Apply as corrections
(the file's open fields are applied, passed fields are left as they were and listed). The record list now carries editable_fields so the
record screen shows "passed, locked" on those fields, and a refused save shows the real reason instead of "Save failed".
Run from the repo root. Safe to run twice."""
